From: dianqk <dianqk@dianqk.net>
Date: Thu, 5 Nov 2026 16:00:00 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] qcom: enable bounded read-only UFS and EFI diagnostics

Use SM8750 GCC/TCSR offsets from the existing Linux source attribution in
0001 (Linux 05441d697f7f9a927264f4058cbbc6a03dfcac9d snapshot).
Keep media write/erase and persistent UFS query changes disabled. Expose
EFI Block IO read-only capability, reserve the RAM transfer buffer and
provide a read-only EFI app that reports protocols/memory then returns.
Fix stale RCG divider bits and propagate UFS initialization failures.
Honor inherited hardware-gated mode for the five UFS CBCR branches, using
Linux clk-branch.c register semantics, without changing the mode:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/05441d697f7f9a927264f4058cbbc6a03dfcac9d/drivers/clk/qcom/clk-branch.c
Host PHY reset uses the Linux ufs-qcom.c register and settling semantics:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/05441d697f7f9a927264f4058cbbc6a03dfcac9d/drivers/ufs/host/ufs-qcom.c
The U-Boot reset provider and driver-model binding are independently adapted.
Initialize the mandatory HC v4+ SYS1CLK_1US before link startup, following
Linux ufs_qcom_cfg_timers. Select core_clk independently from its own OPP
and use the successfully programmed rate; preserve DME setup failures.
Read-only reset, symbol-mux and UIC diagnostics retain cleared interrupt
status across the existing bounded polling loop.
Use the source-supported host PARAM0 maximum for initial SM8750 PHY gear
calibration, independently from the Dodge negotiated link cap of G3. Linux
ufs_qcom_set_phy_gear documents maximum calibration as backward compatible
with lower link gears. Do not change PHY tables or clock rates.
Check Ctrl-C before each SCSI inquiry and report the first SM8750 UTP failure
with bounded status, error and automatic-hibernation diagnostics.
Local changes include compiled multi-clock OPP sizing and bounded transfer
stdio handoff; no Linux clock-branch implementation is copied.
---
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/Kconfig b/arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/Kconfig
index a7cf8b9e..e82ac5b6 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/Kconfig
@@ -2,6 +2,7 @@ if ARCH_SNAPDRAGON
 
 config QCOM_DODGE
 	bool "OnePlus 13 ABL runtime memory handoff"
+	select LMB_LIMIT_DMA_BELOW_RAM_TOP if LMB
 
 
 config SYS_SOC
diff --git a/arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/board.c b/arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/board.c
index 9734cb5e..599702d7 100644
--- a/arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/board.c
+++ b/arch/arm/mach-snapdragon/board.c
@@ -578,6 +578,21 @@ int board_late_init(void)
 	struct fdt_header *fdt_blob = (struct fdt_header *)gd->fdt_blob;
 
 	if (!fdt_node_check_compatible(gd->fdt_blob, 0, "oneplus,dodge")) {
+		bool transfer_valid = false;
+		int i;
+		addr = 0xc0000000;
+		for (i = 0; i < CONFIG_NR_DRAM_BANKS; i++)
+			if (gd->dram[i].start <= addr &&
+			    gd->dram[i].size >= SZ_64M &&
+			    addr - gd->dram[i].start <=
+				    gd->dram[i].size - SZ_64M)
+				transfer_valid = true;
+		if (!transfer_valid ||
+		    lmb_alloc_mem(LMB_MEM_ALLOC_ADDR, SZ_4K, &addr, SZ_64M,
+				  LMB_NOOVERWRITE))
+			panic("Dodge: no safe 64MiB transfer region\n");
+		env_set_hex("loadaddr", addr);
+		env_set_hex("fastboot_addr_r", addr);
 		env_set("board", "oneplus-dodge");
 		env_set("soc", "sm8750");
 		qcom_show_boot_source();
